module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleGlobalGeneration.Twist
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.QcohLimits.Basic

/-!
# Clauses (7) and (8) of Stacks Tag 01Q3, and the dévissage sequence they produce

Stacks Tag 01Q3 is the nine-clause characterisation of ampleness of an invertible module `L` on a
scheme `X`. This file states two of its global-generation clauses,

7. for every quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module `F` **of finite type** there is an `n₀` with
   `F ⊗ L ^⊗ n` globally generated for all `n ≥ n₀`;
8. every such `F` is a quotient of a finite direct sum of copies of `L ^⊗ (-n)` for suitable
   `n > 0`;

and proves that (7) implies (8), in the form of a short exact sequence
`0 → F' → ⊕ⱼ L ^⊗ (-dⱼ) → F → 0` with `F'` quasi-coherent and every `dⱼ ≥ n₀`, as in the dévissage
of [Stacks, Tag 0EBD].

Clause (8) is false for a general quasi-coherent `F`: for `F = ⊕_{i ∈ ℕ} 𝒪_X` on a nonempty `X`,
an epimorphism from a direct sum of `r` invertible modules would give, at a point `x`, a
surjection `𝒪_{X,x}^r → 𝒪_{X,x}^{(ℕ)}`, and tensoring with the residue field gives a surjection of
a finite-dimensional vector space onto an infinite-dimensional one. The finite-type hypothesis is
therefore essential.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.IsEventuallyGloballyGenerated`: clause (7) of Stacks Tag 01Q3,
  for the tensor powers of `L`.
* `Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.IsQuotientOfNegativeTwists`: clause (8) of Stacks Tag 01Q3, as a
  short exact sequence with quasi-coherent kernel and degrees bounded below by any given `n₀`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.exists_shortExact_biproduct_of_generatingSections`: given finitely
  many global sections generating `F ⊗ L ^⊗ n` for a single `n ≥ n₀`, a short exact sequence
  `0 → F' → ⊕_{j : Fin r} L ^⊗ (-dⱼ) → F → 0` with `F'` quasi-coherent and every `dⱼ = n ≥ n₀`.
* `Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration.isQuotientOfNegativeTwists_of_isEventuallyGloballyGenerated`:
  (7) implies (8), Stacks Tag 01Q3.

## Implementation notes

The quasi-separatedness conjunct of the source's clauses (7) and (8) is omitted: it is used in the
source only to prove the clauses from ampleness.

The degrees in clause (8) are a family `d : Fin r → ℤ`; the source uses a single `n`, which is the
constant family.

A family of generating sections is indexed by a type in the module universe `u`, while the direct
sum is indexed by `Fin r`. The index type is moved to `Fin r` by
`CategoryTheory.Limits.Bicone.whisker` along an equivalence `Fin r ≃ σ.I`, with
`CategoryTheory.Limits.Bicone.whiskerIsBilimitIff` transporting the bilimit property. Whiskering
leaves `Bicone.pt` unchanged, so the isomorphism `S.X₂ ≅ b.pt` is `Iso.refl`.

The short complex is `CategoryTheory.ShortComplex.kernelSequence`, whose `X₃` is the target of the
epimorphism, so `S.X₃ = F` holds by `rfl`. Quasi-coherence of the kernel is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QcohLimits.isQuasicoherent_kernel`.

`SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType` quantifies the universe of its local generators existentially, so
the clauses write `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.{u, u, u}` with the universe pinned to the module
universe.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01Q3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Q3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EBD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EBD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01B4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01B4)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits MonoidalCategory
open Stacks.Ample AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules

universe u

namespace Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration

attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafInternalHom.schemeMonoidalCategory
  Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemeBraidedCategory

/-! ### The two clauses -/

variable (X : Scheme.{u}) (L : X.Modules) [IsInvertibleModule X L]

/-- **Stacks Tag 01Q3, clause (7)**, for the tensor powers of `L`: every quasi-coherent
`𝒪_X`-module of finite type becomes generated by finitely many global sections after a
sufficiently positive twist by `L`.

Global generation is Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections`, a family of global sections
whose associated morphism out of the free module is an epimorphism; "finitely many" is the
finiteness of its index type. -/
def IsEventuallyGloballyGenerated : Prop :=
  ∀ F : X.Modules, F.IsQuasicoherent → SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.{u, u, u} F →
    ∃ n₀ : ℤ, ∀ n : ℤ, n₀ ≤ n →
      ∃ σ : (F ⊗ tensorPowModule X L n).GeneratingSections, Finite σ.I

/-- **Stacks Tag 01Q3, clause (8)**: every quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module of finite type is a
quotient of a finite direct sum of negative tensor powers of `L`, of arbitrarily negative degree,
with quasi-coherent kernel. -/
def IsQuotientOfNegativeTwists : Prop :=
  ∀ (n₀ : ℤ) (F : X.Modules), F.IsQuasicoherent → SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.{u, u, u} F →
    ∃ (S : ShortComplex X.Modules) (r : ℕ) (d : Fin r → ℤ)
      (b : Bicone fun j : Fin r => tensorPowModule X L (-(d j)))
      (_ : b.IsBilimit) (_ : S.X₂ ≅ b.pt),
      S.ShortExact ∧ S.X₃ = F ∧ S.X₁.IsQuasicoherent ∧ ∀ j, n₀ ≤ d j

/-! ### The dévissage sequence -/

variable {X L}

/-- **The dévissage sequence of [Stacks, Tag 0EBD], from global generation after one twist.**
If `F` is quasi-coherent and `F ⊗ L ^⊗ n` is generated by finitely many global sections for some
single `n ≥ n₀`, then there is a short exact sequence
`0 → F' → ⊕_{j : Fin r} L ^⊗ (-dⱼ) → F → 0` with `F'` quasi-coherent and every `dⱼ ≥ n₀`. -/
theorem exists_shortExact_biproduct_of_generatingSections
    {n₀ n : ℤ} (hn : n₀ ≤ n) (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    (σ : (F ⊗ tensorPowModule X L n).GeneratingSections) (hσ : Finite σ.I) :
    ∃ (S : ShortComplex X.Modules) (r : ℕ) (d : Fin r → ℤ)
      (b : Bicone fun j : Fin r => tensorPowModule X L (-(d j)))
      (_ : b.IsBilimit) (_ : S.X₂ ≅ b.pt),
      S.ShortExact ∧ S.X₃ = F ∧ S.X₁.IsQuasicoherent ∧ ∀ j, n₀ ≤ d j := by
  have := hσ
  have hπ : Epi (σ.π : freeModule X σ.I ⟶ F ⊗ tensorPowModule X L n) := σ.epi
  obtain ⟨b₀, hb₀, p, hp, hqc⟩ :=
    exists_epi_biproduct_of_epi_free L n F (σ.π : freeModule X σ.I ⟶ _) hπ
  obtain ⟨r, ⟨e⟩⟩ := Finite.exists_equiv_fin σ.I
  have := hp
  have := hqc
  exact ⟨ShortComplex.kernelSequence p, r, fun _ => n, b₀.whisker e.symm,
    (b₀.whiskerIsBilimitIff e.symm).symm hb₀, Iso.refl _,
    ShortComplex.ShortExact.mk' (ShortComplex.kernelSequence_exact p) inferInstance
      (show Epi p from hp),
    rfl, (show (kernel p).IsQuasicoherent from inferInstance), fun _ => hn⟩

/-- **Stacks Tag 01Q3, (7) implies (8).** Global generation of every finite-type quasi-coherent
module after a sufficiently positive twist makes every such module a quotient of a finite direct
sum of negative twists of arbitrarily negative degree, with quasi-coherent kernel. -/
theorem isQuotientOfNegativeTwists_of_isEventuallyGloballyGenerated
    (h : IsEventuallyGloballyGenerated X L) : IsQuotientOfNegativeTwists X L := by
  intro n₀ F hF hFt
  have := hF
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := h F hF hFt
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := hm (max n₀ m) (le_max_right n₀ m)
  exact exists_shortExact_biproduct_of_generatingSections (le_max_left n₀ m) F σ hσ

end Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration

end
